Package: qes-tools
Version: 1.0.9
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Yaroslav Baienko <zerhug@gmail.com>
Depends: nodejs (>= 18), python3 (>= 3.10), python3-cryptography, openssl, zenity, libnotify-bin, qpdf, fonts-liberation, ocrmypdf, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-ukr, tesseract-ocr-eng, unpaper, xdg-utils, libc6 (>= 2.14), libpcsclite1
Recommends: wl-clipboard | xclip, pcscd, libccid, opensc
Provides: eusw (= 1.3.1.109)
Replaces: eusw
Conflicts: eusw (<< 1.3.1.109)
Homepage: https://github.com/YaroslavBaienko/legaltech
Description: Ukrainian Qualified Electronic Signature & Encryption LegalTech Suite
 Offline-first CLI & GUI toolkit for signing, verifying, and encrypting documents
 conforming to Ukrainian DSTU 4145-2002, GOST 28147:89, PKCS#7/CAdES,
 ETSI ASiC-E containers, PAdES (embedded PDF signatures with official visual stamps),
 and asymmetric cryptographic envelopes (qes-encrypt, qes-decrypt).
 Fully integrates IIT End-User CA-1 drivers (eusw, pkcs11.eka1c.so, pkcs11.ekc1.so,
 libav337p11d.so) for native hardware USB tokens (DepositSign Almaz-1K, Crystal-1K,
 SecureToken-337) and browser signing extension (Native Messaging Host).
 Supports auto-discovery across all Ukrainian QTSPs (DepositSign, monobank, Diia,
 Tax Service, PrivatBank, Vchasno, NAIS).
 Preserves attorney-client privilege with 100% offline cryptographic operations.
